    <item>
      <title>Squeak 2.23.20</title>
      <pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 08:51:39 +0000</pubDate>
      <sparkle:version>22320</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.23.20</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <description><![CDATA[<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><style>html{color-scheme:light dark}body{font:13px/1.5 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'SF Pro Text',system-ui,sans-serif;color:#18181b;background:transparent;margin:0;padding:4px 2px}ul{margin:0 0 10px;padding-left:18px}li{margin:0 0 6px}p{margin:0 0 10px}h4{font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:#52525b;margin:16px 0 6px;padding-top:10px;border-top:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,.08)}code{font:12px ui-monospace,'SF Mono',monospace;background:rgba(0,0,0,.06);padding:1px 4px;border-radius:6px}@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){body{color:#f4f4f5}h4{color:#a1a1aa;border-top-color:rgba(255,255,255,.12)}code{background:rgba(255,255,255,.1)}}</style></head><body><ul><li>Full screen no longer shows an empty band at the top.</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.23.19</h4><ul><li>Ducklings run in the background without holding up the thread: a bar shows each one live, click to watch it, and the dashboard counts them.</li><li>Hover hints show below the button (or above it near the bottom), never on top of what you're about to click.</li><li>Shortcuts follow where you're typing, and Squeak shows it: the terminal lights up when it has the keys, and ⌘T there opens a terminal.</li><li>The preset picker says what each preset does — which model leads, which codes, which runs commands — and shows a check on the one you picked.</li><li>Click the context ring to see how full the chat's context is (used and window, percent), and compact it now.</li><li>Squeak for Web now lives on Squeak's own cloud: the pairing QR opens the new address. Browsers paired with the old address pair once more.</li><li>Account and cloud are one card: signing in also connects this Mac to Squeak's cloud.</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.23.18</h4><ul><li>Steering is smooth: your steer shows in the stream and the work carries on below it, nothing folds away.</li><li>Steps stay in time order around your steer: what happened before it above the card, what came after below.</li></ul></body></html>]]></description>
